Institute, Bulgarian Academy of Sciences) and V. Benghin (Institute of Biomedical Problems, Russian Academy of Sciences), http://esa-pro.space.bas.bg/datasources/LIULIN_MO. Reference: Semkova et al., Icarus 303, 53–66 (2018).","retrievedAt":"2026-11-15T12:28:16.289Z"},"note":"Columns \"Dose AB\" and \"Dose CD\" of the source: the absorbed dose rate in silicon in the two detector pairs, which point in two perpendicular directions. The source has one value for each hour. It does not name the unit. We read it as µGy for each hour, because the means of the file then agree with the paper of the instrument team (file: 371 and 389 µGy for each day, paper: 372 ± 37 and 390 ± 39). A daily value is the mean of the hourly values of one UTC day, times 24 hours, divided by 1000. \"total\" is the mean of the two detectors. A day with fewer than 12 hourly values is null (no data): the instrument was off from 19 July to 11 August 2016 and was on only at times after that. On 3, 4, and 5 June 2016 the source holds each hourly value two times. We keep one (71 lines removed). The source gives times with no zone. We read them as UTC. The orbiter left the Earth on 14 March 2016. \"missionDayOfStart\" is the count of days from that date to the first value."}